{
  "model": "faster-whisper small / cpu int8",
  "elapsed_seconds": 14.424777567000092,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.04,
      "text": " I started with a phone and a lot of questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.14,
      "end": 5.72,
      "text": " Could I build my own AI operating system without coding?"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.16,
      "end": 11.56,
      "text": " First, I learned the parts, a model to think, tools to act, skills to guide it, and saved"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.56,
      "end": 12.06,
      "text": " context."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.56,
      "end": 13.46,
      "text": " Then I built a router."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.6,
      "end": 16.56,
      "text": " New information goes to the right specialist."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.56,
      "end": 19.58,
      "text": " I call these specialists my elders."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.08,
      "end": 21.24,
      "text": " The router points the way."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.28,
      "end": 26.36,
      "text": " It loads the useful context instead of dumping every note into every answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.74,
      "end": 27.58,
      "text": " I stay the chief."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.36,
      "end": 35.0,
      "text": " small, reversible jobs can move ahead. Real choices come to my desk, where I decide."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.58,
      "end": 40.34,
      "text": " The quartermaster helps pick the tools. The architect helps organize the system."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.4,
      "end": 45.38,
      "text": " Their work becomes something I can use, but a confident answer isn't proof."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.34,
      "end": 51.18,
      "text": " We plant faults and check the result. I'm still proving the foundation's work."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.62,
      "end": 54.94,
      "text": " Next, help a friend build their own system and document it."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.94,
      "end": 57.36,
      "text": " One useful step at a time."
    }
  ],
